  "description": "The `return` cell of `an-every-handler-stop-is-not-consumed-by-its-registering-call`, which carries the rationale. `return` is the signal spec/execution-model.md:660-664 names explicitly — a value-carrying escape is the one a live caller frame could actually absorb as its own result — so it raises `ol-return-outside-proc` (spec/error-model.md:116) while `setup` is still on the stack. Separate from its `stop` sibling because the runtime converts the two signals in two adjacent branches at each of the four handler sites, so a mutant can remove either one alone; and separate from every other fixture because execution stops at the first diagnostic. The `return` trace event is still emitted by the statement before the boundary reclassifies the escaping signal.",
